@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-keeps-card-order
The library mosaic MUST preserve the server's card order and every card ID when it
lays cards out. At two to four columns cards share square cells in bands of one or two
rows, filled row by row, as Google Photos breaks up its squares: screenshots and other
tall pictures stand two squares high, about half the wide pictures lie two across, and
about one picture in seven is big, two by two, chosen by the card's id so it keeps its
shape across reloads. Text, posts and pictures with words take one square. A band MUST
NOT leave a hole before the last card. One column shows each card across the width at
its own proportions. Images fill their cells; text cards retain a readable preview. Tap
and hold MUST target the same card at every density.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, Google Photos layout request in the Codex conversation;
the recorded review of 23 October 2026 ("they use all these shapes to break up the
layout so that you don't just have like a bunch of squares", "the screenshots are kind
of taking the aspect ratio of screenshots", "some of these images are just bigger").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-mixed-cards-keep-text-and-images
A note, social post, article or saved link with text and a picture MUST show both in its gallery
preview, including the smallest density and Top of Mind. Neither the cover nor a
generated title may replace the note or post body. Text and images MUST have separate
visible areas, and text MUST use the app's font with enough contrast against its paper. A
photo or video with an authored note MUST also retain that note beside its image.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, preserve text and images in small note previews.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] gallery-pinches-change-tile-size
A two-finger pinch on the mosaic MUST continuously change tile size through multiple
density levels and reverse while the fingers remain down. Density stops
MUST offer distinct sizes for uniform portrait, square and landscape cards, with one
to four columns at their stops. Text MUST retain its size and wrapping when
releasing at a stop. A tile with words MUST be a picture of itself: it is laid out
once, one square wide at three columns in the shape of its cell, and drawn scaled
to its cell at every density and between them, so it MUST NOT rewrap, change its
inset, or show or hide its labels while the fingers move (Tavi, 28 Oct 2026: notes
"still shift weirdly" when pinching; he picked version 13 of the design canvas).
Adjacent cached grids MUST remain coherent and nonoverlapping within each projection, sharing one focal card's fractional X/Y point and physical
size. Each stop holds briefly before the fingers move on, and the grid shown between
two stops MUST be the denser one enlarged, never a sparser one shrunk below its size,
so no empty band appears. A crossing starts a 250 ms handoff in which every card glides
from its place in the old grid to its place in the new one, never a crossfade of
two grids. When a tile with words changes shape between the two grids (one column
against two), it fades from its old layout to its new one within its moving cell,
the only time a card is drawn twice, and the old layout exposes no semantics or hit
targets. The gallery then MUST show one grid even if the fingers pause or jitter at
the threshold. Reduced motion switches the grid
immediately. Apart from that fade, the focal card MUST be drawn once and only one
projection may expose semantics or hit targets. A new single-finger press
MUST retain its owning projection and focal node through tap or hold. Passing drag
slop releases focal anchoring; a second finger rebases a new pinch. A press during a
handoff holds every card where it is until the press ends.
Vertical anchoring respects scroll bounds. The focal point stays where the fingers
met: moving both fingers together MUST NOT pan the gallery. At every moment of a
gesture the projected grid MUST cover the full width, clipping its outer edges
rather than leaving horizontal slack. The profile and
highlights keep their own scale. Release MUST settle the same geometry without an
independent row animation; reduced motion settles synchronously. The gesture, its
cancellation and a remaining one-finger tail MUST NOT open a card, open its action
sheet, or trigger pull to refresh. Rendering MUST retain stable card keys and a lazy,
bounded visible window, without scanning all cards or changing image decode sizes
on each pointer frame. Equivalent larger/smaller actions MUST be accessible, and
each tab MUST retain its density and scroll position. Removing the gallery during
a gesture or settle MUST synchronously save a canonical density and anchored scroll
request, so reusing its state cannot restore a fractional transition.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, explicit pinch-to-enlarge/reduce requirement; the
recorded review of the same day, with Google Photos as the reference ("the
intermediate state where there is emptiness", "I shouldn't be able to pan"); the
recorded review of 23 October 2026 ("then they reorganize completely, which is weird
and doesn't feel good").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-highlights-stay-above-the-bricks
Top of Mind MUST remain above the main mosaic, in pin order, as a horizontal rail of
large highlight cards. The rail MUST remain horizontally scrollable and scroll
vertically with the mosaic, without a visible "Top of Mind" text heading. Profile
and highlights MUST NOT scale with a mosaic pinch.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, Google Photos layout request and gallery polish in the Codex conversation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-top-controls-stay-fixed
The profile, Add and Rediscover controls MUST stay fixed at the top of Everything and
the Spaces list while the page scrolls under them. They float as their own raised,
shadowed circles with no solid header strip behind them. The page title ("Your
mind", "All Spaces") MUST scroll away with the page. The controls MUST remain
available for an empty, loading or failed feed. Pull to refresh and mosaic gestures
belong to the scrolling page; search and browsing MUST retain independent scroll
positions.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, gallery polish in the Codex conversation; the recorded
review of the same day ("the title should not be sticky", "the buttons should be
sticky but without a background").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;interaction] gallery-top-edge-blurs-the-scrolling-content
Once the page has scrolled, the cards passing under the status bar and the fixed
controls MUST soften through true backdrop blur that fades into the sharp viewport;
at the top of the page there is no blur. It MUST sample the displayed
gallery rather than create a second feed or replace the cards with an opaque
gradient. The fixed controls stay sharp, and the decorative blur MUST NOT own taps,
pinches or pull-to-refresh gestures.
Source: Tavi's annotated gallery screenshot, 22 October 2026: "We're missing blur
on the top part of the scrollable section."

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] spaces-share-the-gallery-page
The Spaces list and an opened space MUST use the gallery's background, title row and
floating controls, not a separate page style. Spaces MUST NOT have a floating create
button: New space is offered in the Add sheet opened from the Spaces list, and
adding to or deleting an opened space lives in that space's options menu.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("the background should be the same",
"remove the orange plus, but keep the functionality").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] gallery-videos-play-quietly
Video tiles MUST NOT show a camera icon. A video kept on the library server MUST play
muted and looping in its tile while the app is in front and system animations are on,
at most three at once, over its still until the first frame shows; one saved without a
cover MUST show a still the server takes from the video, never an empty "Video" tile.
Videos on other sites such as YouTube keep their still cover. Every video tile with a
picture MUST show the Google Photos corner badge: the length (m:ss, or h:mm:ss) once a
player has read it and the tile has room, then a white play circle, drawn straight on
the picture with a soft shadow, with no pill and no site logo. Previews MUST only
request media from the library server.
Source: Tavi's recorded reviews, 22 October 2026 ("I don't really like this camera icon",
"videos autoplay ... They don't play with sound", "this icon with the time is actually
much more helpful") and 23 October 2026 ("that YouTube icon, if you look at the Google
Photos ... it was a lot more interesting", "the videos aren't auto playing").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-posts-look-like-posts
A social post tile MUST read as the post itself: the platform, the post's words, its own
picture inset with rounded corners below them, and the author when the tile has room.
Bare media links the platform appends, such as pic.twitter.com or t.co addresses, MUST
NOT appear as text in the tile or the reader.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("if we have a link for the thing, I
don't think we should put it on the thing", "I think we can just probably show the tweet").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] gallery-text-is-one-size
All gallery tile text MUST use one size and one regular weight, so neighbouring tiles
read alike; only a highlight card's text is larger. Long text wraps with hyphenation and
fills the tile before it is cut with an ellipsis; it never shrinks to fit. A tile's kind
label MUST NOT repeat the words shown under it, such as a link whose only text is its
own address. That size is the tile's at three columns; at other densities every tile
with words is drawn scaled with its cell (gallery-pinches-change-tile-size), so the
tiles of one grid still read alike.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 23 October 2026 ("some fonts are bigger, some fonts are
smaller ... this is just weird", "some of them are bold"), replacing the shrinking text
of 22 October; scaling with the cell from Tavi's pick of version 13, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;privacy] gallery-repositories-have-covers
A GitHub repository card without a stored cover MUST show GitHub's generated preview
picture of that repository. Requests to any host other than the library server MUST NOT
carry the session token (`data/Api.kt` AuthInterceptor).
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("repositories I think could use having
the repositories cover").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;privacy] gallery-opens-from-the-phone
Everything, Top of Mind and the page scheme MUST open on what they showed last time,
read from the phone's own copy (`data/LibraryCopy.kt`), before the server answers. The
server's first page then decides: when the list already starts with it, the list stays
and paging goes on after it; otherwise the list becomes the fresh page. Without the
network the kept cards stay on show. The copy holds at most the first
200 cards of each list, belongs to the session that wrote it, reads as empty under any
other session and is wiped at sign-out; a copy that cannot be read or written MUST
never stop the app.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, the plan "ThyMind: instant app and better search", step 2
(an instant, offline local copy on the phone).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;privacy] gallery-works-offline
Once the phone holds the whole library (`data/LibraryCopy.kt`, filled page by page from
`/app/v1/changes` by `data/LibrarySync.kt`), Everything, Top of Mind, the Spaces tab and
its covers, space pages and the cards Serendipity deals MUST read from it, in the
server's order, without waiting on the network. Space pages read from it only once its
cards carry their place in the space (`spaceRanks`); before that they ask the server.
Pull to refresh on the Spaces tab or in a space syncs the copy first. The copy syncs
when the app starts, comes back to the screen, regains internet, is pulled to refresh,
and after each successful change. Without internet the app MUST stay usable: no blocking
screen, a small Offline pill under the top controls, and search by words, cards, spaces
and space pages answered from the copy. A server without the changes feed MUST leave the
app working as before. The copy belongs to its session and is wiped at sign-out, like
`gallery-opens-from-the-phone`.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, the plan "ThyMind: instant app and better search", step 3
(sync and offline mode); spaces, space pages and Serendipity added for Tavi's ask of 28
October 2026 for a sync engine like Zero in Omar's Wholana, plan "ThyMind: a Zero-style
sync engine", step 1.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;privacy] gallery-keeps-offline-changes
A pin, trash, note, tag or space change to a card MUST show on the phone at once and read
as done, online or not: it waits in the phone's copy (`data/Outbox.kt`) and reaches the
server in the background, in the order it was made, even with the app closed. A card added
to a space shows at the end of it. Waiting changes MUST go out together through the
server's push, each under its place in the queue, so the server applies a change sent
twice only once; a server without the push gets them one by one. A change the server
refuses is dropped, its card read again, and a short notice names the card. Only while the
server answers that it has no changes feed does an online change go straight to the
server. Waiting changes belong to the session and are wiped at sign-out. New cards,
uploads and creating or deleting spaces still need a connection.
On Wi-Fi with battery to spare, the phone MUST fetch ahead the gallery pictures of Top of
Mind and the newest 1,000 cards (`data/KeptPictures.kt`) into its picture cache, which
holds up to 512 MB and is wiped at sign-out with the copy.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, the plan "ThyMind: instant app and better search", step 4,
and his choice of "Pinned + newest 1,000, Wi-Fi" for the pictures; online changes queued
first for Tavi's ask of 28 October 2026 for a sync engine like Zero in Omar's Wholana, plan
"ThyMind: a Zero-style sync engine", steps 2 and 3.
